titre$ Tuomikoski – C Y S T O D E R M E S
Com$ Nordic Macromycetes II, 1973 – adapté par Paul Bertéa 05-02-2011
1,2 $ Ring persistent, membranous, sheathed below, with granulose underside and filamentous upper surface, cap finely granulose. Cystidia absent; sp amyloid
1,5 $ Ring evanescent, with granulose veil extending down the stem

2,0 $ Cap and stem pale lilaceous or pink to almost white; smell and taste unpleasant. Sp 4-5.5 x 3-5 µm (Fig. 127); KOH hardly discolouring cuticular cells of cap. - Mossy forests, needle beds, heaps of debris; especially late autumn. D&D 321, MLge, R&H 420. $ C. carcharias (Pers.) Konr. & Maubl.
2,3 $ Cap and stem rusty ochraceous; smell and taste not distinctive. KOH discolouring the cuticular cells dark rusty brown

3,0 $ Cap rusty brown (rarely medium brown or ochre), distinctly granulose. Sp 4-5 x 3-3.5 µm , mostly broadly ellipsoid to subglobose (Fig. 128). – Mossy forests. SZP 35: 117, M&J III Calocybe 4. $ C. fallax Smith & Sing.
3,4 $ Cap ochre or fulvous brown , finely granulose. Sp longer than above

4,0 $ Frb fairly slender; cap ochre; stem with fairly narrow ring. Sp 5-6 x 2.5-3.5 µm, ellipsoid. $ C. intermedium Harmaja
4,0 $ Frb stouter; cap slightly brighter, fulvous brown; ring fairly broad. Sp 5-7 x 3.5-4.5 µm, mostly broadly ellipsoid to subglobose. $ C. tuomikoskii Harmaja

5,6 $ Sp amyloid. Cap yellowish or brownish ochre to dark brown
5,8 $ Sp non-amyloid

6,0 $ Stem apex, above the annular zone, pale purple to dark violet when fresh, intensely violet when dry; frb small, cap pale to dark brown without yellowish tinge, surface very finely granulose; flesh pale without yellow tinge. Sp ± fusoid, 6-7.5 x 3.5-5 µm. - Among mosses (esp . Polytrichum), esp. on rock outcrops, also in bogs; late in the season . BSMF 89 pl 1. $ C. lilacipes Harmaja 
6,0,N$///(= C longisporum (Kuhn.) Heinem. & Thoen var. purpurascens Heinem. & Thoen nom. inval.).///C. saarenoksae Harmaja differs esp. in yellow brown colours.///C. niveum Harmaja differs esp. in being white
6,7 $ Stem apex yellowish to brownish, rarely with a faint purplish tinge at least when dry

7,0 $ Flesh of cap distinctly yellow in upper part, otherwise ochre; cap yellowish brown or paler; gills yellow. Sp 6-7.5 x 3-5 µm, ± fusoid (Fig. 130); arthrospores abundant in upper part of cap flesh. - Mossy forests. D&S 320, lower right fig., Cke 1113/ 935, R&H 421. $ C. jasonis (Cooke & Massee) Harmaja 
7,0,N$///(= C. amianthinum var. longisporum Kühn.)
7,0 $ Flesh white throughout; cap brown to yellowish, granules often small; gills whitish. Sp 5-7 x 2.5-3 µm, ellipsoid to oblong (Fig. 126); arthrospores lacking or rare. - Among mosses in forests and heaths. D&D 320 (upper row), Phil 31, R&H 420. $ C. amianthinum (Scop.) Konr. & Maubl.

8,0 $ Frb snow white, at least when young; cap with pointed scales which soon fall away. Sp 4-5.5 x 2.5-3 /µm (Fig. 125). - Forests and bogs, among mosses. Bres 50. $ C. ambrosii (Bres.) Sing.
8,9 $ Frb coloured

9,0 $ Cap dark rusty to vinaceous brown, fading to pale sordid brownish. Sp 3.5-5 x 2.5-3 µm (Fig. 129). - Forests and heaths, roadsides, rarely in bogs. MLge, Mossb II 65 , R&H 421. $ C. granulosum (Batsch:Fr.) Kuhn.
9,10 $ Cap some shade of red or orange

10,0 $ Cap brownish cinnabar to reddish orange; stem often stout, with subbulbose base and usually with copious patches of the red velar coating at least at and below annular zone. Sp 3.5-5 x 2-3(-3.5) µm (Fig. 131); cystidia slightly vcntricose below, tapering to a long, narrow neck with spear-shaped apex often covered with crystals. - Forests, among mosses or on needle beds. FAD 15 F, R&H 422 , C 411. $ C. terrei (Berk. & Br.) Harmaja 
10,0,N$///(= C cinnabarinum (Alb. & Schw.) Konr. & Maubl.)
10,0 $ Cap bright reddish orange to orange yellow; stem usually more slender, below annular zone mainly coated by the pure white filamentous inner velar layer, coloured velar remnants small and scarce, mostly situated near the base; gills more broadly adnate, even subdecurrent. Sp 3.5-4.5 x 2.5-3 µm ; cystidia absent. - Mossy ground in forests. Miller 110 (sub C. amianthinum). $ C. adnatifolium (Peck) Harmaja 
10,0,N$///(= C. granulosum var. adnatifolium (Peck) Smith & Sing.)
